 to $x\\in R$ with the Fourier series shown above. What is the $6\\text{th}$ Fourier cosine coefficient of $5f(x)+2g(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ be $2\\pi $-periodic functions with Fourier series\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)), \\\\ g(x) & ∼\\frac{{c}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({c}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{d}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen for any constants $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $,\n\n$$\n\\alpha f(x)+\\beta g(x)∼\\frac{\\alpha {a}_{0}+\\beta {c}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }((\\alpha {a}_{n}+\\beta {c}_{n})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+(\\alpha {b}_{n}+\\beta {d}_{n})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nUsing the linearity property of Fourier series, the corresponding Fourier coefficients of $5f(x)+2g(x)$ are\n\n- $5{a}_{0}+2{c}_{0}$ for the constant coefficient,\n\n- $5{a}_{n}+2{c}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1$ for the cosine coefficients, and\n\n- $5{b}_{n}+2{d}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1$ for the sine coefficients.\n\nTherefore, the $6$th cosine coefficient of $5f(x)+2g(x)$ is\n\n$$\n5{a}_{6}+2{c}_{6}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354650 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb295d6c-62fe-59bc-a139-49785ac98f1f" :knowledge-point/title "Using Linearity of Fourier Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f60ebf3-5b0e-5ffa-94fb-9b96cd365132" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4{b}_{1}+{d}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354652} {:answer/id #uuid "e96dcb88-36a7-5d3b-be98-7414919fe89a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{a}_{0}+4{c}_{0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354653} {:answer/id #uuid "13cb8951-469c-56e6-87d7-f0dca0c4b468" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{0}-4{c}_{0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354654} {:answer/id #uuid "be54c098-aa19-578a-aecb-c4e4f947409e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{b}_{1}+4{d}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354655} {:answer/id #uuid "44ee4074-4502-57da-9e30-bbf4c05a1305" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4{a}_{0}+{c}_{0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354656}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e96dcb88-36a7-5d3b-be98-7414919fe89a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{a}_{0}+4{c}_{0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354653} :answer-field/id #uuid "54915c80-05c0-50ab-a32d-0c9e1cea2ca0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354651}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4fa14996-0471-53d5-a75c-e87949c2f5ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-340762" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx) \\\\ g(x) & ∼\\frac{{c}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{c}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{d}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ be $2\\pi $-periodic extensions of some functions from $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ to $x\\in R$ with the Fourier series shown above. What is the constant Fourier coefficient of $-f(x)+4g(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ be $2\\pi $-periodic functions with Fourier series\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)), \\\\ g(x) & ∼\\frac{{c}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({c}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{d}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen for any constants $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $,\n\n$$\n\\alpha f(x)+\\beta g(x)∼\\frac{\\alpha {a}_{0}+\\beta {c}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }((\\alpha {a}_{n}+\\beta {c}_{n})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+(\\alpha {b}_{n}+\\beta {d}_{n})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nUsing the linearity property of Fourier series, the corresponding Fourier coefficients of $-f(x)+4g(x)$ are\n\n- $-{a}_{0}+4{c}_{0}$ for the constant coefficient,\n\n- $-{a}_{n}+4{c}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1$ for the cosine coefficients, and\n\n- $-{b}_{n}+4{d}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1$ for the sine coefficients.\n\nTherefore, the constant Fourier coefficient of $-f(x)+4g(x)$ is\n\n$$\n-{a}_{0}+4{c}_{0}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354657 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb295d6c-62fe-59bc-a139-49785ac98f1f" :knowledge-point/title "Using Linearity of Fourier Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6e5f5a3-6e6f-5425-b40d-40e41ea905d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{b}_{4}-2{d}_{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354659} {:answer/id #uuid "5fd288d9-f217-519a-a0bc-67d8462b7532" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{a}_{0}-2{c}_{0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354660} {:answer/id #uuid "093a7e71-1fc6-5a2d-b344-3e83ae4ad0a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{b}_{4}-2{c}_{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354661} {:answer/id #uuid "e0042157-1449-5e32-9ba4-67b444803d68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{a}_{4}-2{c}_{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354662} {:answer/id #uuid "3cd04719-16f5-5fea-8a2a-95d280c3826e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{b}_{0}-2{d}_{0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354663}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6e5f5a3-6e6f-5425-b40d-40e41ea905d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{b}_{4}-2{d}_{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354659} :answer-field/id #uuid "79dd5213-8ef0-5738-839d-70014b81edd8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354658}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "40fa711d-c9dc-564e-b6fc-b6cb743edecf" :question/math-academy-id "q-340766" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx) \\\\ g(x) & ∼\\frac{{c}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{c}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{d}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ be $2\\pi $-periodic extensions of some functions from $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ to $x\\in R$ with the Fourier series shown above. What is the $4\\text{th}$ Fourier sine coefficient of $3f(x)-2g(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ be $2\\pi $-periodic functions with Fourier series\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)), \\\\ g(x) & ∼\\frac{{c}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({c}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{d}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen for any constants $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $,\n\n$$\n\\alpha f(x)+\\beta g(x)∼\\frac{\\alpha {a}_{0}+\\beta {c}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }((\\alpha {a}_{n}+\\beta {c}_{n})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+(\\alpha {b}_{n}+\\beta {d}_{n})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nUsing the linearity property of Fourier series, the corresponding Fourier coefficients of $3f(x)-2g(x)$ are\n\n- $3{a}_{0}-2{c}_{0}$ for the constant coefficient,\n\n- $3{a}_{n}-2{c}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1$ for the cosine coefficients, and\n\n- $3{b}_{n}-2{d}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1$ for the sine coefficients.\n\nTherefore, the $4$th sine coefficient of $3f(x)-2g(x)$ is\n\n$$\n3{b}_{4}-2{d}_{4}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354664 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb295d6c-62fe-59bc-a139-49785ac98f1f" :knowledge-point/title "Using Linearity of Fourier Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93a209b6-dc8c-5bd6-8ac9-d5758018552a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{b}_{7}+2{d}_{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354666} {:answer/id #uuid "250ef3d6-b876-539e-94d7-cfea03b74