rname{cos}⁡(nx)+{d}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen for any constants $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $,\n\n$$\n\\alpha f(x)+\\beta g(x)∼\\frac{\\alpha {a}_{0}+\\beta {c}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }((\\alpha {a}_{n}+\\beta {c}_{n})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+(\\alpha {b}_{n}+\\beta {d}_{n})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nUsing the linearity property of Fourier series, the corresponding Fourier coefficients of $5f(x)+2g(x)$ are\n\n- $5{a}_{0}+2{c}_{0}$ for the constant coefficient,\n\n- $5{a}_{n}+2{c}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1$ for the cosine coefficients, and\n\n- $5{b}_{n}+2{d}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1$ for the sine coefficients.\n\nTherefore, the $7$th sine coefficient of $5f(x)+2g(x)$ is\n\n$$\n5{b}_{7}+2{d}_{7}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354671 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f30ca427-3074-56c3-828a-1327d7b172b0" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Effects of Vertical Shifting and Horizontal Reflection on Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5ca71e0-4f51-5aa2-9127-2cd9d9bf9b74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{0}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354673} {:answer/id #uuid "4cb47fb5-39b8-5e39-b4ea-dc21f290eb02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354674} {:answer/id #uuid "9c73c6c2-67e3-5bfd-bc70-81a22420539b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{0}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354675} {:answer/id #uuid "923e030b-e4d4-5a72-9baa-3c165339cec0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{0}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354676} {:answer/id #uuid "dd50ff20-47a8-5e58-84b9-45497061ecc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{0}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354677}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd50ff20-47a8-5e58-84b9-45497061ecc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{0}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354677} :answer-field/id #uuid "4dd2e828-3e15-500e-b52b-3c8288844890" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354672}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e65aca98-124d-51f8-a741-9ec96636d29c" :question/math-academy-id "q-340778" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of a function from $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ to $x\\in R$ with the Fourier series shown above.  What is the constant Fourier coefficient of  $f(x)+1?$" :question/worked-solution "The Fourier series of $f(x)$ is\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx).\n$$\n\nRecall that if $C$ is a constant, the corresponding Fourier coefficients of $f(x)+C$ are\n\n- ${a}_{0}+2C$  for the constant coefficient,\n\n- ${a}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1,$ for the cosine coefficients, and\n\n- ${b}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1,$ for the sine coefficients.\n\nIn our case, $C=1.$ Therefore, the constant Fourier coefficient of $f(x)+1$ is ${a}_{0}+2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354678 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f30ca427-3074-56c3-828a-1327d7b172b0" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Effects of Vertical Shifting and Horizontal Reflection on Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b29e75f5-3ae6-5bb7-8ae3-e19dab7bea0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{b}_{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354680} {:answer/id #uuid "94ed8318-ae6c-5344-98e1-7ff585cc551f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{b}_{4}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354681} {:answer/id #uuid "97ec3c84-4149-5596-8e95-78a286703d3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{a}_{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354682} {:answer/id #