xt} :answer/value "sine terms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354711} {:answer/id #uuid "98b66ab4-9a49-58d8-b944-2b46d501515e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "cosine terms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354712}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd31a030-f578-5894-9cd3-f8c6ad46de0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "sine terms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354711} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a32e46f-5938-59af-bafa-76f422850638" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354710}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2741ca02-a0ca-568b-9994-9ebcd5878556" :question/math-academy-id "q-340797" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-{x}^{2}$ on $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ].$ Select the correct options below.\n$\\,$\nThe function $f(x)$ is\n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$\nConsequently, the {{field-2}}\nin the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x)$ must be zero." :question/worked-solution "To check whether $f$ is even or odd, we compare $f(-x)$ and $f(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-x)-(-x)^{2} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-{x}^{2} \\\\  & =f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f(-x)=f(x),$ we have that $f$ is even.\n\nFor the Fourier series on $[-\\pi ,\\pi ],$ the sine coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, $f(x)$ is even and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)$ is odd, so $f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)$ is odd.\n\nNow, the integral of an odd function over $[-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ is $0.$ Thus, ${b}_{n}=0$ for all $n\\ge 1.$\n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ is $\\text{even}$ and the $\\text{sine terms}$ in its Fourier series must be zero."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354713 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "532a73e6-e026-57c9-9bad-57cd2f75b6df" :knowledg