$f(-x)$ and $f(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & ={sin}^{2}⁡(-x)+5 \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))^{2}+5 \\\\  & ={sin}^{2}⁡(x)+5 \\\\  & =f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f(-x)=f(x),$ we have that $f$ is even.\n\nFor the Fourier series on $[-\\pi ,\\pi ],$ the sine coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, $f(x)$ is even and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)$ is odd, so $f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)$ is odd.\n\nNow, the integral of an odd function over $[-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ is $0.$ Thus, ${b}_{n}=0$ for all $n\\ge 1.$\n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ is $\\text{even}$ and the $\\text{sine terms}$ in its Fourier series must be zero."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354720 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "532a73e6-e026-57c9-9bad-57cd2f75b6df" :knowledge-point/title "Parity Recognition and Series Type"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2dcb8280-7169-5501-91ed-dca90eb21eb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "even" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354722} {:answer/id #uuid "1373085a-ed8e-5b1c-8181-825eebded0de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "odd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354723}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1373085a-ed8e-5b1c-8181-825eebded0de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "odd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354723} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f691013-78ed-50c3-bcc8-28eff43c37bd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354721} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95426d33-5078-5aac-a53c-9063b70b0548" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "sine terms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354725} {:answer/id #uuid "6f40bf76-2ca5-5fdb-aa42-0e4983bd5f31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "cosine terms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354726}] :answer-field/correct 